EXT. ROOFTOP WATER TOWER - SUNSET

A rusted ladder, a patched tank. Four teens sit on the catwalk with feet dangling. The town below is small and gold.

JUNIPER LOPEZ, 16, plays with a bottle cap. WESLEY "WES" CHUKWU, 17, eats sunflower seeds. DELPHINE ABERNATHY, 16, writes in a notebook. TOMAS KOWALCZYK, 15, lies flat, staring up.

WES
(to everyone)
Last summer before everything changes.

JUNIPER
(to Delphine)
You're going, right? To the city?

DELPHINE
Maybe.

TOMAS
(to himself)
Clouds look like nothing.

Juniper flicks the bottle cap over the rail. It disappears.

WES
Somebody say something deep.

TOMAS
The tank's leaking.

They all look down. A thin trickle runs along the catwalk. Nobody moves.
